Key implementation details for node-level duplicate detection:
```python
def dup_keys(text):
    node = yaml.compose(text)
    dups=[]
    def walk(n):
        if isinstance(n, yaml.MappingNode):
            seen={}
            for k,v in n.value:
                if isinstance(k, yaml.ScalarNode):
                    key=k.value
                    if key in seen:
                        dups.append({"key":key,"first_line":seen[key],"again_line":k.start_mark.line+1})
                    else:
                        seen[key]=k.start_mark.line+1
                walk(v)
        elif isinstance(n, yaml.SequenceNode):
            for c in n.value: walk(c)
    walk(node)
    return dups
```
This handles the rev26 duplicates correctly (once each).

